    "turn_text": "Hello and welcome to this special edition of the American Forecast. Today we speak to Nancy Pelosi, one of the most consequential figures in American politics in recent history, arguably the most powerful woman ever in American politics. Now, while she's never run for president, she's managed to accumulate and wield a vast amount of power in Washington, DC. She became the first woman to hold the very influential speaker of the House position, the third most influential position in America after the President and the Vice President. And she's been amongst the top power brokers in the Democratic Party for decades, when endorsement from her could make or break careers. Well, she's just released a book called The Outer Power, and she joins me now. Madam Speaker, it's wonderful to have you in the programme. You write a lot in your book about the mail club of the House of Representatives, an institution that you have served in since 1987, that you adore and cherish, but it was, for many years, a mail club. And here you made history. You know, back in the day when he became the first female speaker, but also you might be about to see history being made with Kamala Harris becoming the first female president of the United States. Now, you saw her in San Francisco. How confident is she that she's going to make history? Well, I think she's",
