    "turn_idx": 101,
    "turn_text": "I'm very solution-oriented. And what she was saying, actually, in the fuller context was that when she was 16 years old, I asked for her permission for me to run for Congress because we have five children, four of them were already in college. She was only going to be a senior in high school, young for senior year, but nonetheless. So I said, Mommy, has been asked to run for Congress. I don't know if I'll win, but I wouldn't even consider it if you didn't think it would be okay. And I went on to say that Mommy would be gone three nights a week when Congress was in session. She responded by saying, mother, not Mommy, mother, get a wife. I had never heard that expression. That became a common lingo, but I hadn't heard it. I was first, get a life. What teenage girl wouldn't want her mother out of the house three nights a week? So she was harkening back to that, saying if I had known that this would end up with a hammer on dad's head, I would never have agreed to your going forward. And if I had known, it would end up with that action that I would never have proceeded. But we've got to get the job, John, and the best way to do that is to make sure we have a political solution. We make sure that we win this election. And I'm stronger to do that where I am.",
